-- title:
--   Cyclotomic extension with uniformiser 1-ζ_q, all primes q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a natural number assumed prime, and let $Z_0$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the principal ideal generated by $q$. The assertion is the existence of a type $V$ carrying a commutative ring structure making it a domain and a discrete valuation ring, together with a $Z_0$-algebra structure under which $V$ is finite and free as a $Z_0$-module, an implication asserting that the residue field of $V$ is finite whenever that of $Z_0$ is, an element $\varpi \in V$ generating the maximal ideal of $V$ and with $Z_0[\varpi]$ the whole of $V$ (the $Z_0$-subalgebra generated by $\{\varpi\}$ equals $\top$), a unit $\varepsilon \in V$ with $\varpi^{q-1} = \varepsilon q$, and the relation $\sum_{i<q}(1-\varpi)^i = 0$; and, finally, the universal property: for every commutative ring $R$ with a $Z_0$-algebra structure and every $\zeta \in R$ satisfying $\sum_{i<q}\zeta^i = 0$, there is a $Z_0$-algebra homomorphism $\iota : V \to R$ with $\iota(\varpi) = 1-\zeta$.
--
--   This produces the cyclotomic base $Z_0[\zeta_q]$ over a discrete valuation ring ramified exactly at $q$, presented through the uniformiser $\varpi = 1-\zeta_q$ together with its universal property for $q$-th roots of unity; it is the version with no lower bound on $q$, so that the prime $q = 2$ is included. It is used in the construction of unramified identifications of completions of modular-curve function fields in the analysis of the fibre at $q$.
